# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example
# `.env.*` above also matches `.env.example`, and `!.env.*.example` does not
# rescue it (that pattern needs a segment between the dots, e.g. .env.dev.example).
# The template MUST be tracked — it is the only non-secret record of which
# variables exist. Found 25 Jul 2026 when the Laravel scaffold landed and the
# skeleton's .env.example silently disappeared from git's view.
!.env.example

# Laravel
.phpunit.result.cache
/.phpunit.cache
auth.json

# Secrets
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
*_password*.txt
*_token*.txt

# Dependencies (future app code)
vendor/
node_modules/

# Build artifacts
public/build/
storage/*.key
bootstrap/cache/*.php

# OS/editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Project-specific expectations (stakeholder MVP, not code)
ekspektasi-user

# Agent config (per AGENTS.md M-3)
# Trailing `/*` rather than `/` so git still descends into the directory and
# the negation below can take effect — a blanket `.claude/` ignore makes any
# `!.claude/...` rule unreachable. settings.json still matches this line and
# stays ignored, which is the point of M-3.
.claude/*

# Un-ignored 8 Aug 2026, same reasoning as `!ekspektasi-user` below: these are
# shared project knowledge, not local agent config. `.claude/skills/kiro-*`
# encode this repository's Kiro spec workflow (kiro.dev/docs/specs) together
# with the AGENTS.md rules that override it — useless to a teammate or to CI
# if they live only on one machine. Kiro's own best practice is the same:
# spec tooling belongs in the repository beside the specs it governs.
!.claude/skills/

# Un-ignored 8 Aug 2026, same reasoning as the skills above. Subagent role
# definitions double as agent-team teammate types
# (code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-teams), and Claude Code's own guidance is to
# "check them into version control so your team can use and improve them
# collaboratively". They are project knowledge, not machine-local config.
# .claude/settings.json deliberately stays ignored (AGENTS.md M-3) — the
# CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS flag lives there and is a per-machine
# opt-in into an experimental feature, not a project decision.
!.claude/agents/

# Reversed 25 Jul 2026: this line un-ignores ekspektasi-user despite the
# blanket ignore above. Reasoning recorded in the commit message and in
# docs/planning/ekspektasi-vs-specs.md §4 D5 — it is the stakeholder-MVP
# expectation document, authority rank 2 under AGENTS.md, and its being
# untracked broke CI (GATE 4: a link to it 404s on a clean checkout).
!ekspektasi-user

# MCP config (may contain DB URLs)
.mcp.json

# Superpowers subagent-driven-development isolated workspaces (scratch git
# worktrees, one branch per in-flight plan) — never committed.
.worktrees/
